From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:27:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] uloop: do not pass exit() requests to the exception guard

Since the exception guard was added, uc_uloop_vm_call() hands every
exception of a callback to the guard handler, also the EXCEPTION_EXIT
that exit() raises. The guard receives an "Exit" exception and the loop
keeps running. When run() returns, the script ends with code 0 instead
of the code given to exit(), because the VM already reset its call
frames for the exit request.

End the loop and keep the exit request pending, as without a guard, so
that the script terminates with the requested code.

Fixes: aaf712eb4fb4 ("uloop: add guard() function")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 create mode 100644 tests/custom/06_lib_uloop/12_callback_exit

--- a/lib/uloop.c
+++ b/lib/uloop.c
@@ -149,9 +149,17 @@ uc_uloop_vm_call(uc_vm_t *vm, bool mcall
 {
 	uc_value_t *exh, *val;
 
-	if (uc_vm_call(vm, mcall, nargs) == EXCEPTION_NONE)
+	switch (uc_vm_call(vm, mcall, nargs)) {
+	case EXCEPTION_NONE:
 		return true;
 
+	case EXCEPTION_EXIT:
+		goto error;
+
+	default:
+		break;
+	}
+
 	exh = uc_vm_registry_get(vm, "uloop.ex_handler");
 	if (!ucv_is_callable(exh))
 		goto error;
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/custom/06_lib_uloop/12_callback_exit
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+Calling exit() in a uloop callback ends the loop and terminates the script
+with the given code, also when an exception guard is set. The guard does not
+receive the exit request.
+
+-- Testcase --
+{%
+	import * as uloop from 'uloop';
+
+	uloop.init();
+
+	uloop.guard((e) => print(`guard: ${e.type}\n`));
+
+	uloop.timer(10, () => exit(4));
+	uloop.timer(100, () => {
+		print("loop kept running\n");
+		uloop.end();
+	});
+
+	uloop.run();
+	print("run() returned\n");
+%}
+-- End --
+
+-- Expect exitcode --
+4
+-- End --
